WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:02.804
(techno music)

00:00:38.001 --> 00:00:40.251
(rap beat)

00:01:07.002 --> 00:01:10.535
- [Trap House] Okay, there's some beats.

00:01:10.535 --> 00:01:13.080
(Beats)

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.435
(Laughing)

00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:18.807
Hip-hop allows you to be the
voice for the voiceless.

00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:22.081
When I met Isaiah, I
didn't know what to expect.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:25.597
Once I had an opportunity
to communicate with him,

00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:27.985
I was like, nah, he can talk.

00:01:27.985 --> 00:01:28.978
He can talk.

00:01:28.978 --> 00:01:30.529
He has no problem talking.

00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:32.715
Let's figure out how we
want to end this song out.

00:01:32.715 --> 00:01:33.660
How we want to close it out.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.278
When I think of Isaiah as an artist,

00:01:35.278 --> 00:01:37.693
I more-so feel that he's a poet.

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:40.625
He's writing poetry, he's
talking about his experiences.

00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:43.181
♫ I don't care what people think of me.

00:01:43.181 --> 00:01:44.458
♫ Proud and honored that they carry me.

00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:48.312
♫ Jaw gone but I love myself,
like a lion to my family.

00:01:48.312 --> 00:01:49.145
♫ Heart big...

00:01:49.145 --> 00:01:52.299
The first thing that Isaiah
and I did was Oxygen to Fly.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:54.716
He wrote it, I was the voice.

00:01:55.894 --> 00:01:58.020
It's a challenge to be
someone else's voice,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.537
but Isaiah has so many
things that he wants to say,

00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:03.333
we find a way to make it work.

00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.744
(Laughing)

00:02:04.744 --> 00:02:06.520
Yeah, yeah, okay.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.291
Next we can work on the second verse.

00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:11.596
Before I worked with Isaiah,
I had a heavy presence

00:02:11.596 --> 00:02:14.548
in the local scene as far as rap music

00:02:14.548 --> 00:02:17.159
as well as some community work.

00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:17.992
- [Music Director] All right,

00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:19.226
we're going to take it from the top, ok.

00:02:19.226 --> 00:02:21.917
- [Trap House] We were
able to come together and

00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:24.394
kind of amplify our message and that's

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:27.178
just that you shouldn't stand to the side

00:02:27.178 --> 00:02:29.615
and do nothing if you're fully
capable of doing something.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:32.236
I brought out a special guest tonight man,

00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:34.125
his name is Isaiah the Rapper.

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:36.514
Ya'll do me a favor and make
some noise for my boy Isaiah.

00:02:36.514 --> 00:02:37.374
(Cheering)

00:02:37.374 --> 00:02:40.041
(Soulful music)

00:03:01.528 --> 00:03:04.195
(Rapping music)

